### [05:56:30 UTC] Step 2 — Hypothesize
Hypothesis A (e2e adaptive-filter gap): No existing test runs upscale() end-to-end with toggle_adaptive_filter=True, so a wiring regression in the block-adaptive lms_filter path within upscale() (feed.py:752-766) -- e.g. wrong axis, shape mismatch, or numerical instability at real pipeline data -- would go undetected by the whole suite even though the underlying lms_filter unit tests pass. Since source review shows the wiring is a straightforward per-channel lms_filter(channel, channel) call with defaults, I predict a new e2e test with toggle_adaptive_filter=True, small max_iterations, and the existing small synthetic-sine mp3 fixture will PASS (finite/non-silent/low-clipping/440Hz-dominant output), positively confirming (not just failing to disconfirm) that the fix from cycle 1 (block_size=256) is correctly wired end-to-end -- closing the coverage gap either way.
Hypothesis B (block_size=1 equivalence / iteration-count gap): lms_filter's own docstring claims (1) block_size=1 reproduces the exact prior per-sample update algebraically, and (2) the block-adaptive rewrite cuts sequential Python-loop iterations from n to ~n/block_size, with default block_size=256 -- none of this is asserted by any test. I predict: (a) an independent per-sample-loop reference implementation of the exact same update rule (same w-init, same delay convention, same 2*mu*e*x term, no block averaging) will match lms_filter(..., block_size=1) output and final weights closely (cp.allclose), confirming the equivalence claim; (b) instrumenting _lms_block_ranges call counts during a real lms_filter run will show block_size=256 performs ceil((n-start)/256) sequential iterations vs exactly (n-start) at block_size=1 -- a ~2-orders-of-magnitude reduction -- confirming the speedup claim; and default block_size is 256 per inspect.signature. If any of these mismatch, that's a real defect in the block-adaptive math/wiring to fix, not a test to weaken.
Reasoning: Per scientific-coding.md, hypothesis + prediction must precede any file edit. Both target the exact two gaps enumerated in the task (test-fat-llama's audio_quality failures for test_feed_covers_adaptive_filter_end_to_end and test_feed_covers_block_lms_equivalence_and_iteration_count).
